### `Consent banner flips global mode`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| AUTO + consent-missing banner → user taps Grant → global mode becomes VPN | Banner reused `requestVpnAndStart()` which calls `setGlobalMode(VPN)` | Banner: `requestVpnConsent()` = `VpnService.prepare()` + `orchestrator.refresh()` only; segmented VPN chip keeps full `requestVpnAndStart()` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `M3 Expressive needs alpha BOM`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `ExperimentalMaterial3ExpressiveApi` / `MaterialExpressiveTheme` unresolved, or lint KaCall after a BOM-only bump | Stable `compose-bom` maps material3 **1.4.0** (Expressive removed). BOM-only bump on older AGP mismatches lint's Kotlin analysis API | `compose-bom-alpha` + material3 1.5.0-alpha on AGP **9.2** / `compileSdk 37`. Opt in per screen. Do not BOM-only bump on AGP 8.x. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Proxy network row shows em-dash`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Network row `Status: —` while PROXY is up and joined | ViewModel reads only the VPN stack's per-network list; proxy join state lived only inside the libzt node manager | Both runtimes publish `NetworkRuntimeStatus` on their `StateFlow`; ViewModel resolves via `plan.runtime` + `resolveNetworkRuntime` — never hard-wire VPN-only |

